+| Render identity inventory agrees with converter identity scopes, quoted names, source origins and normative library identities without RDF emission. | `NewDeclarationElementIDsInModel`, `renderidentity.BindInventory` | `TestDeclarationIdentityInventoryPreservesScopesAndNormativeIDs`, `TestModelDeclarationsMatchesFullCrossDocumentConversion` | Implemented; native identity facts are authoritative. |
+| Native requirement context uses an explicit deterministic depth frontier; depth zero is induced selection and bounded views preserve directed dependencies. | `RequirementContext`, `requirementContextDepth`, `generalGraph.relate` | `TestRequirementContextDepthIsDeterministic`, `TestRequirementContextInducedSelectionAndLegacy`, `TestRequirementContextRejectsInvalidDepth`, `TestDOTEdgeKinds` | Implemented as an OpenSysML rendering extension; legacy unannotated views retain existing behavior. |
+
+
+## General-view relationship identity
+
+General views retain one edge per source declaration, endpoint pair, kind and
+label. Distinct parallel assertions therefore retain distinct source origins and
+canonical semantic identities through native JSON rendering; repeated discovery
+of the same declaration does not duplicate its edge. This is rendering identity,
+not a claim that satisfaction assertions are executed or accepted.
+
+| Contract | Implementation | Verification | Status |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Distinct source declarations survive identical endpoints and labels | `internal/ir/view/general.go:generalGraph.add` | `TestGeneralGraphDeduplicatesBySourceOrigin`, `TestGeneralViewParallelSatisfactionOrigins` | ✅ faithful |
+| Parallel satisfaction identities remain stable across cached identity-enabled and ordinary requests | `internal/frontend/engine` rendering and native identity binding | `TestRenderParallelSatisfactionIdentities` | ✅ faithful |
+
+Edges whose producing declaration is not located retain the existing endpoint,
+kind and label deduplication. The renderer does not invent a source identity for
+such artifacts.
